1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,011
A public website, such as a help center, is knowledge that an assistant can read.

2
00:00:06,011 --> 00:00:09,871
This video shows how a web crawler reads a site page by page,

3
00:00:09,871 --> 00:00:14,652
keeps the knowledge current on a schedule, and lets the assistant answer with

4
00:00:14,652 --> 00:00:16,380
a link back to the page.

5
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:25,132
Much of what customers ask is already answered on your website:

6
00:00:25,132 --> 00:00:28,200
shipping times, warranty terms, account help.

7
00:00:28,950 --> 00:00:33,987
Copying those pages into the assistant by hand takes time, and the copies

8
00:00:33,987 --> 00:00:36,920
go stale as soon as the website changes.

9
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:41,928
A web crawler reads the website page by page on a schedule, and

10
00:00:41,928 --> 00:00:46,000
turns each page into passages that the assistant can search.

11
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:51,584
Only new, changed and removed pages are processed, and the sources under an

12
00:00:51,584 --> 00:00:54,210
answer link back to the original page.

13
00:00:58,410 --> 00:01:03,930
A knowledge base index stores the passages, so the assistant can search them by meaning.

14
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:06,757
A Web data source is the target:

15
00:01:06,757 --> 00:01:09,600
the knowledge that the assistant answers from.

16
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:12,393
A web crawler is the reader.

17
00:01:12,393 --> 00:01:16,780
The Sitemap strategy finds the pages of a site through its sitemap.

18
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:21,632
Then you choose the data source on a profile, and the assistant answers

19
00:01:21,632 --> 00:01:23,390
from the pages, with links.

20
00:01:27,588 --> 00:01:35,168
Open Search, Indexes, click Add index, and click Add on AI Knowledge Base Index for Elasticsearch.

21
00:01:36,113 --> 00:01:41,561
Enter an Index Name and a Name, pick the Embedding deployment, and click Save.

22
00:01:41,561 --> 00:01:47,853
Data sources, file sources and web crawlers store their passages in an index like this one.

23
00:01:52,072 --> 00:01:58,035
Open Artificial Intelligence, Data Sources, click Add Data Source, and click Add on Web.

24
00:01:58,035 --> 00:02:00,572
It is the target for web crawlers.

25
00:02:01,029 --> 00:02:07,682
Enter a Name, and choose the Destination index, the knowledge base index that stores the passages.

26
00:02:07,682 --> 00:02:10,369
It cannot be changed after you save.

27
00:02:10,823 --> 00:02:11,879
Click Save.

28
00:02:11,879 --> 00:02:16,103
The data source is listed, and waits for a crawler to fill it.

29
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:25,330
Open Artificial Intelligence, Web Crawlers, and click Add Web Crawler.

30
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:29,130
In Available Crawl Strategies, click Add on Sitemap.

31
00:02:29,601 --> 00:02:34,782
Enter a Name, and choose the Target Web data source, the one you just made.

32
00:02:34,782 --> 00:02:38,171
Several crawlers can feed the same data source.

33
00:02:38,667 --> 00:02:41,268
Base URL is the website to read.

34
00:02:41,268 --> 00:02:44,417
The crawler finds its sitemap by itself.

35
00:02:44,417 --> 00:02:49,277
Sitemap URL is optional, for a sitemap that lives somewhere else.

36
00:02:49,741 --> 00:02:53,024
Max pages is the most pages read in one run.

37
00:02:53,024 --> 00:02:57,817
Max concurrent requests is how many pages are read at once, so keep

38
00:02:57,817 --> 00:03:00,509
it low to be polite to the website.

39
00:03:00,509 --> 00:03:04,121
Request timeout is how long to wait for one page.

40
00:03:04,576 --> 00:03:10,149
Include URL patterns and Exclude URL patterns choose which pages to read, one

41
00:03:10,149 --> 00:03:12,902
pattern per line, and Exclude wins.

42
00:03:12,902 --> 00:03:17,536
User-Agent is how the crawler introduces itself to the website.

43
00:03:17,991 --> 00:03:21,985
Keep Enabled ticked, so that the crawler runs on its schedule.

44
00:03:21,985 --> 00:03:26,213
Re-index interval is how often the site is read again, in minutes.

45
00:03:26,213 --> 00:03:27,211
Click Save.

46
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:35,789
To read the website right away, open the Actions menu of the crawler

47
00:03:35,789 --> 00:03:37,679
and click Synchronize now.

48
00:03:42,425 --> 00:03:44,885
The crawler runs in the background:

49
00:03:44,885 --> 00:03:47,765
it reads the sitemap, and then every page.

50
00:03:47,765 --> 00:03:52,685
Only new, changed and removed pages are processed, so the next run is quick.

51
00:03:52,685 --> 00:03:57,065
When it is done, the pages are knowledge that an assistant can use.

52
00:04:01,266 --> 00:04:06,136
Open the profile, open the Knowledge tab, and choose the data source.

53
00:04:06,608 --> 00:04:11,659
Restrict answers to retrieved data only keeps the assistant to your website.

54
00:04:11,659 --> 00:04:14,061
When nothing matches, it says so.

55
00:04:14,061 --> 00:04:15,108
Click Save.

56
00:04:19,303 --> 00:04:22,131
Now ask a question that the website answers:

57
00:04:22,131 --> 00:04:24,563
how long does standard shipping take?

58
00:04:25,033 --> 00:04:28,323
The assistant answers from the page that the crawler read.

59
00:04:28,792 --> 00:04:32,992
Under the answer, the numbered source shows the page, and links to it.

60
00:04:37,192 --> 00:04:38,336
A help center:

61
00:04:38,336 --> 00:04:42,112
customers get answers from the articles you already publish.

62
00:04:42,862 --> 00:04:44,001
Product pages:

63
00:04:44,001 --> 00:04:47,762
the assistant knows what each product does, and links to it.

64
00:04:48,512 --> 00:04:50,214
Public documentation:

65
00:04:50,214 --> 00:04:53,932
developers ask a question and land on the right page.

66
00:04:54,682 --> 00:04:55,958
Keep it polite:

67
00:04:55,958 --> 00:05:01,182
read only websites you may read, and keep the number of concurrent requests low.

68
00:05:03,182 --> 00:05:07,169
Create the index and a Web data source, point a web crawler at

69
00:05:07,169 --> 00:05:11,977
a website, and the assistant's knowledge follows the pages, with links back.

70
00:05:11,977 --> 00:05:13,502
Thanks for watching.

